I want to add a parser to the input of apoc.mgr.mineGraphRule(), the parser should take a string formatted in a certain way and translate into the current input structure. The string is formatted like this:
"MINE GRAPH RULE <name>
GROUPING ON (<anchorVariable>:<anchorLabel>)[WHERE <anchorWhere>]
DEFINING BODY AS <bodyItemset>
	 HEAD AS <headItemset>
[WHERE <whereConditions>]
[IGNORE <ignoredVariable1>[, <ignoredVariable2>]]
EXTRACTING RULES WITH SUPPORT > <minSupport> AND CONFIDENCE > <minConfidence>"

where the terms within <> can change and are the actual inputs (except > after SUPPORT and > after CONFIDENCE), and you have that elements in between square brackets [] that are optional so they might not be in the string. <bodyItemset> and <headItemset> are constructed equalty and are defined recursively as <Itemset> := <pattern> or <pattern>, <itemset>. <patter> is constracted as <pattern> := [1..<n>](<anchorVariable>)<relPattern><patternTail> [AS <patternName>] When <n> is not given it is assumed as 1. the <patternTail> is defined recursively as <patternTail>:=(<variable>:<nodeLabel>) or (<variable>: <nodeLable>)<relPattern><patternTail>. <relPattern> might be three different relationship patterns: 1) <singleRel> := -[:<relType>]-> where relType is a relationship type. 2) <any>:=-[]->{1, <pathLength>} where pathLenght is an int. 3) <countRel> = -[<relType>>= <mincount>]-> where <relType> is a relationship type and <mincount> an int (there is >= that symbols more than). 

